    # `duplicate fn ... last definition wins` is easy to read as benign shadowing, and
    # usually is. It is not benign when the two definitions disagree about ARITY, because
    # the duplicate path routes AROUND the call-site arity check that has been a hard error
    # since v6.5.1: measured at 6.5.36, a 3-arg call bound to a 1-arg duplicate compiled and
    # ran, silently dropping arguments 2 and 3 (exit 201 where 106 was intended), while the
    # identical mismatch with no duplicate present is refused outright. This is the one way
    # to defeat that check.
